{
  "dom_id": "step-q139965",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $C$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $A$ and $B$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$A$  and $B$ only.\"",
